@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Recorded readings — public lookup/playback and retained upload contracts
hide empty members
class SnapshotModel <<reference>>
class ReadingLookup {
  text: str {nonblank, length=1..4000}
  language: fr | en
  lookup_key(): str
}
class ReadingConsent <<retained>> {
  share_consent: true
  explicit_consent(value): bool {class}
}
class ReadingUpload <<retained>>
class ReadingRecord {
  id: CanonicalUUID
  audio_filename: safe generated filename
  created_at; updated_at: Timestamp
}
class ReadingView {
  audio_url: str
}
class ReadingSearch
class StoredReading {
  id: CanonicalUUID
  key: 64-character SHA-256 hex
  consistent_identity(): Self
}
class Ownership <<reference>>
ReadingLookup --|> SnapshotModel
ReadingConsent --|> SnapshotModel
ReadingUpload --|> ReadingLookup
ReadingUpload --|> ReadingConsent
ReadingRecord --|> ReadingLookup
ReadingView --|> ReadingRecord
ReadingSearch --|> SnapshotModel
StoredReading --|> SnapshotModel
ReadingView "0..*" --> "1" Ownership : ownership
ReadingSearch "0..*" --> "0..1" ReadingView : reading
StoredReading "0..*" --> "1" ReadingRecord : data\nJson[ReadingRecord] after validation
note bottom of ReadingLookup
  Key = SHA-256(language + NUL + normalized text).
  Unicode/case/apostrophe normalization and collapsed spaces
  share a reading; punctuation and language stay distinct.
  Missing reading returns reading=null, never generated audio.
end note
note bottom of ReadingConsent
  Multiple inheritance is implemented by ReadingUpload.
  Consent is a legacy upload-input requirement, not a public
  capture feature or retrospective proof about existing audio.
end note
legend bottom
  Source: backend/readings_models.py. Public routes: POST /api/readings/lookup; GET /api/readings/{id}/audio.
  Existing audio may be played/downloaded. Public create/replace/delete are denied.
  No browser TTS, microphone capture, automatic transcription or cloned voice is in this public workflow.
endlegend
@enduml
